  "description": "The 2026 election for Massachusetts's 3rd Congressional District will determine who represents the district covering northeastern and central Massachusetts, including Lowell and Lawrence, in the U.S. House of Representatives. Incumbent Democrat Lori Trahan, first elected in 2018 and re-elected unopposed in 2024, is running for a fifth term. The district is considered safely Democratic by major nonpartisan forecasters. The Republican primary candidate is retired U.S. Army Colonel Gary Grossi, and unenrolled candidate Kevin Ades is also running in the general election. The primaries are scheduled for September 1, 2026.",
